oe UI Symbol","Noto Color Emoji";font-size:calc(16px + .2vw);color:var(--color-text);line-height:calc(1.4 * var(--body-line-height-multiplier));font-weight:400;}</style><div class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-1sp3kvx"><div class="css-1dhrrqj-BlockTextField"><div class="text align-left-mobile "><p>"I was born and raised in the northwest suburbs of Chicago in an immigrant, Catholic, Indian-American family. My Mother worked for the U.S. Postal Service for more than 20 years and my Father attended night school at DePaul becoming a software engineer. My brothers and I worked hard, did well in school, had the classic Midwestern upbringing. To put it simply, I have always felt that my family and life experience has been a physical testament to the American Dream.</p><p>That same American Dream that was afforded to me and my family has been beginning to fall apart. I've seen it personally with friends struggling to find jobs, neighbors wrestling with healthcare bills, and the halls of Government that are starting to crack.</p><p>I'm running for Congress because we can't afford to wait anymore. The old way of doing things <em>isn't </em>working, but <strong>we can make things better</strong> if we work together and find practical solutions. It's time to try something new, and it's time to try something real."</p></div></div></div><style data-emotion="css 1wg6t9t-Signature">.css-1wg6t9t-Signature{position:relative;display:-webkit-box;display:-webkit-flex;display:-ms-flexbox;display:flex;-webkit-box-pack:start;-ms-flex-pack:start;-webkit-justify-content:flex-start;justify-content:flex-start;margin:0;}.css-1wg6t9t-Signature:not(:last-child){margin-bottom:1.5em;}@media (max-width:766.95px){.css-1wg6t9t-Signature{-webkit-box-pack:center;-ms-flex-pack:center;-webkit-justify-content:center;justify-content:center;margin:auto;}}</style><div class="css-1wg6t9t-Signature"><svg width="17.488704042167537vw" height="4.851423268626251vw" viewBox="0 0 360.4860486048605 100" p