d in the suburbs of Chicago that feels the American Dream is still out there. For all of us.\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-right image-tilt-left\" style=\"width: 45%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/6a95a818-7c5e-4f89-8e53-1678954f56ff/6a95a818-7c5e-4f89-8e53-1678954f56ff.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=0%2C0%2C2645%2C2088\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"right\" alignwidth=\"45\" tiltdirection=\"left\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003ch3\u003e\u003cspan style=\"color: var(--color-text)\"\u003eBorn and raised in the American Dream...\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI was born in Des Plaines, raised in Hoffman Estates, and currently live in South Barrington. \u003c/strong\u003eMy parents immigrated here from India in the 1990s, my mom worked the night shift at the Post Office for more than 20 years and my dad took classes at DePaul, while working full-time to become a software engineer. To put it simply, I can't think of a better example of the American Dream than the story of my family.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eInvolved in our Community...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-left image-tilt-right\" style=\"width: 35%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/14fe2ddd-7f93-4c8d-8050-18808a2cb0ff/14fe2ddd-7f93-4c8d-8050-18808a2cb0ff.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=0%2C0%2C3023%2C3301\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"left\" alignwidth=\"35\" tiltdirection=\"right\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI graduated from Barrington High School, \u003c/strong\u003ewhere I spent most of my time as a Varsity Wrestler and volunteering at Holy Family Catholic Church as a 5th Grade Sunday School teacher. \u003ca href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1VjXaV2pdk5W_3-lkGZC3QCNwW7fXYl5c/view?usp=share_link\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eCongressman Krishnamoorthi\u003c/a\u003e and Senator Durbin chose to nominate me with my applications to the U.S. Air Force and Naval Academies. Over the summers and during the school year, I worked as a\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eLifeguard\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e at Hoffman-Estates Park District\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eMechanic\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e at the Route 62 Auto Shop on Algonquin Rd\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eServer\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e at the Lucky Monk near AMC\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eKindergarten/Preschool Teacher\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e at Crème De Le Crème\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003ch4\u003eWorking through College...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-right image-tilt-left\" style=\"width: 35%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/e71aa464-a15c-4d11-8055-593c4e1dc107/e71aa464-a15c-4d11-8055-593c4e1dc107.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=184%2C217%2C3366%2C2564\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"right\" alignwidth=\"35\" tiltdirection=\"left\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI spent the next years at the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign, \u003c/strong\u003ewaking up at 6 a.m. for morning workouts as an ROTC cadet, leading a \u003ca href=\"https://ugresearchjournals.illinois.edu/index.php/IJOIS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eResearch Journal\u003c/a\u003e as \u003cstrong\u003eEditor-in-Chief\u003c/strong\u003e, and paying for school by working as a \u003cstrong\u003eResident Advisor\u003c/strong\u003e. With a lot of hardwork and many sleepless nights, \u003cstrong\u003eI graduated in two years, \u003c/strong\u003eas a sophomore, in the top 3% of my class, all in the middle of a Global Pandemic.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eTo working overseas...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-left image-tilt-left\" style=\"width: 35%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/510c4b00-8893-46ea-b1b2-d2467160d8cd/510c4b00-8893-46ea-b1b2-d2467160d8cd.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=0%2C0%2C4032%2C3024\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"left\" alignwidth=\"35\" tiltdirection=\"left\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI went overseas with the Fulbright Program, \u003c/strong\u003eworking as a High-School English Teacher in Salzburg Austria. But aside from rounding up a classroom of teenage boys, I learned how a country and a system with progressive policies \u003cstrong\u003eactually worked. \u003c/strong\u003eThings like universal healthcare, robust education, and a dynamic transportation system. Practical solutions I'm ready to take back to Capitol Hill.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eFrom Policy to Practice...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-right image-tilt-left\" style=\"width: 37%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/75675017-1a0b-4be4-9ece-ba4787d283cd/75675017-1a0b-4be4-9ece-ba4787d283cd.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=149%2C409%2C4698%2C3153\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"right\" alignwidth=\"37\" tiltdirection=\"left\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI came back home for graduate school at The University of Chicago, \u003c/strong\u003eearning a Masters in International Politics. I conducted research on \u003ca href=\"https://d3qi0qp55mx5f5.cloudfront.net/cpost/i/docs/Pape_-_Remorse_Report_(2022-09-14).pdf?mtime=1664821905\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eJan 6th\u003c/a\u003e, was a Graduate Fellow at World Business Chicago focusing on Technology and Innovation, Taught a course on Counterterrorism and wrote my \u003ca href=\"https://knowledge.uchicago.edu/record/7243\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eGraduate Thesis\u003c/a\u003e on the Rule of Law.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eU.S. Dept. of Justice...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image image-framed image-left image-tilt-left\" style=\"width: 50%;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-inner-wrapper\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/ed9d52da-4a8d-4716-a432-d7520c3173a7/ed9d52da-4a8d-4716-a432-d7520c3173a7.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026amp;bri=0\u0026amp;con=0\u0026amp;sat=0\u0026amp;high=0\u0026amp;shad=0\u0026amp;usm=0\u0026amp;rect=0%2C0%2C750%2C422\u0026amp;w=1500\" alt=\"\" caption=\"\" align=\"left\" alignwidth=\"50\" tiltdirection=\"left\" variant=\"framed\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"caption\" style=\"display: none\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI moved to D.C. as part of the Presidential Management Fellows Program,\u003c/strong\u003e where I began work at the Justice Dept.'s National Security Division - Counterterrorism Section. It was my job to prevent and respond to Domestic and International Terrorist attacks - I hold a Top Secret Clearance and \u003cstrong\u003emy office was responsible for prosecuting the January 6th insurrectionists\u003c/strong\u003e, the Abbey Gate terrorist attack in Afghanistan, and numerous School Shootings across the country.\u003c/p\u003e\u003ch4\u003eConsider this my Resignation...\u003c/h4\u003e\u003cp\u003eI always wanted to pursue a career in public service. This nation gave so much to me and my family that it was an honor to serve, and when I got to the Justice Dept. I was proud of the work I was doing.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBut over time, I saw things I couldn’t ignore: career professionals pushed out, due process disregarded, and political influence creeping into places it doesn’t belong. I tried to convince myself that staying inside the system was the best way to help fix it. But at some point, I had to ask whether staying silent made me part of the problem.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eI resigned\u003c/strong\u003e because I decided it wasn't worth staying silent anymore. I'm running for congress because I think it's time for people with integrity to step up - and that we need more people in Washington who will defend the rule of law, not bend it.\u003c/p\u003e","bgColor":"bg0","callout":"DATA_DETAILS","eyebrow":"Eyebrow Text Here","headline":"Headline Text Here","marginTop":"top-large","headlineOn":false,"quoteImage":"https://media.designedtorun.com/415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202/1656059613254-1655837013629-fortune-vieyra-xdmtQVVKibU-unsplas-smaller-gigapixel--.jpg","description":"Description Text Here","eyebrowSize":0,"showEyebrow":false,"calloutItems":[{"id":"c0ec8280-cae3-4d0b-999f-2eb4f932dd3e","title":"Born","value":"Categories can be edited in the sidebar"},{"id":"212d58d2-da79-4e03-a10b-8b870959f442","title":"\u003cp\u003eRaised\u003c/p\u003e","value":"Put where you grew up here"},{"id":"838a601f-b009-41dc-bb98-83cd29313ac8","title":"\u003cp\u003eMarried\u003c/p\u003e","value":"Put year here"},{"id":"a837d8e4-b41f-44f2-b49e-5f9ee8216744","title":"\u003cp\u003eChildren\u003c/p\u003e","value":"List children and maybe their ages"},{"id":"2d6958c0-7863-4b9b-9f96-a357f406aee7","title":"\u003cp\u003eParty\u003c/p\u003e","value":"Put party here"},{"id":"25a0fb25-c50c-46d2-957d-c55d5a171371","title":"\u003cp\u003eEducation\u003c/p\u003e","value":"Put degree and school here"}],"headlineSize":0,"marginBottom":"bottom-large","calloutBgColor":"bg3","descriptionSize":5,"showDescription":false},"type":"BASIC_TEXT","title":"Text","pageId":"1f04f73e-4282-4e13-951a-80f26d67ec47","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":"CUSTOM","createdAt":"2025-05-29T18:52:51.671+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":"797be3f2-d419-46f4-bff0-ca14d79e6f61","postStructure":[],"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"f140abb8-de9f-4051-b4f3-01c4f08df350":{"id":"f140abb8-de9f-4051-b4f3-01c4f08df350","data":{"text":"\u003cp\u003e\"I was born and raised in the northwest suburbs of Chicago in an immigrant, Catholic, Indian-American family. My Mother worked for the U.S. Postal Service for more than 20 years and my Father attended night school at DePaul becoming a software engineer. My brothers and I worked hard, did well in school, had the classic Midwestern upbringing. To put it simply, I have always felt that my family and life experience has been a physical testament to the American Dream.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThat same American Dream that was afforded to me and my family has been beginning to fall apart. I've seen it personally with friends struggling to find jobs, neighbors wrestling with healthcare bills, and the halls of Government that are starting to crack.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eI'm running for Congress because we can't afford to wait anymore. The old way of doing things \u003cem\u003eisn't \u003c/em\u003eworking, but \u003cstrong\u003ewe can make things better\u003c/strong\u003e if we work together and find practical solutions. It's time to try something new, and it's time to try something real.\"\u003c/p\u003e","image":"https://media.designedtorun.com/415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202/1653539254769-iStock-1348963486---runcbt::0,cbl::89.26223776223776,cbw::524.4755244755245,cbh::300,d::1662850989909,o::https:--slash----slash--media.designedtorun.com--slash--415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202--slash--1653539254769-iStock-1348963486-.jpgrun--.jpg","bgColor":"bg0","buttons":[{"id":"a30acdcb-0344-4cb4-a030-8403ef7cae7f","url":"","buttonUrl":"","buttonText":"Learn More"}],"heading":"\u003cp\u003eThis moment demands leaders from a \u003cu\u003eNew Generation\u003c/u\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","embedCode":"","imageTilt":"tilt","marginTop":"top-large","layoutType":"TWO","imageBorder":"border","twoColImage":"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/4bbc5243-9d3a-4ba2-bde4-cdd0030c49d9/4bbc5243-9d3a-4ba2-bde4-cdd0030c49d9.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026bri=0\u0026con=0\u0026sat=0\u0026high=0\u0026shad=0\u0026usm=0\u0026rect=0%2C1831%2C2729%2C3800","bodyCopySize":-10,"hasImageTilt":true,"imageAltText":"Introductory photo","marginBottom":"bottom-large","showHeadline":true,"showSignature":true,"hasImageBorder":true,"signatureImage":"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/fd11aa07-b89c-4cd9-a742-5a284b8ef76a/7dbb6081-464a-46b5-8b81-899de61108aa.webp?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026bri=0\u0026con=0\u0026sat=0\u0026high=0\u0026shad=0\u0026usm=0\u0026rect=35%2C28%2C4005%2C1111","showDescription":true,"showFeaturedLink":false,"signatureAltText":"Candidate signature","introHeadlineSize":-5},"type":"INTRO","title":"Page Intro","pageId":"a7f662cc-5e1d-4248-9a11-7068425e37f8","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":"HOMEPAGE_MAIN","createdAt":"2025-05-29T18:52:51.671+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":"70bbd268-1b17-4a68-bc41-530efecbba2b","postStructure":[],"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"46504484-1f0b-4ad5-aa40-14fca1a6ce6a":{"id":"46504484-1f0b-4ad5-aa40-14fca1a6ce6a","data":{"html":"\u003ciframe width=\"1000\" height=\"500\" frameborder=\"0\" scrolling=\"no\" marginheight=\"0\" marginwidth=\"0\"\nsrc=\"https://www.govtrack.us/congress/members/embed/mapframe?state=il\u0026district=8\u0026bounds=-88.837,42.528,-87.471,41.484\"\u003e\u003c/iframe\u003e","bgColor":"bg0","marginTop":"top-large","marginBottom":"bottom-large","disablePadding":false},"type":"EMBED","title":"Embed","pageId":"5eb75eea-2f2a-43e8-9c8d-e6a83d28f2b6","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":null,"createdAt":"2025-05-30T19:15:26.75137+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":null,"postStructure":null,"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"17da85a7-00d9-49a5-9997-be6b4ae0773f":{"id":"17da85a7-00d9-49a5-9997-be6b4ae0773f","data":{"bgColor":"bg0","marginTop":"top-large","showEyebrow":true,"marginBottom":"bottom-large"},"type":"ISSUE_SINGLE","title":"Issues Post","pageId":"1590c9e9-1c9d-42b8-83e5-37e0df32a5f6","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":null,"createdAt":"2025-05-29T18:52:51.671+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":null,"postStructure":[],"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"690611a2-eb6e-48bb-a3d1-447fed9caf11":{"id":"690611a2-eb6e-48bb-a3d1-447fed9caf11","data":{"text":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003e\"Let's hit the mat, and get to work.\"\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","image":"https://run.imgix.net/f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee/e1b96832-504b-487d-a997-3a2e051b91ee/e1b96832-504b-487d-a997-3a2e051b91ee.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026bri=0\u0026con=0\u0026sat=0\u0026high=0\u0026shad=0\u0026usm=0\u0026rect=0%2C0%2C2048%2C1365","bgColor":"bg3","marginTop":"top-large","layoutType":"QUOTE_IMAGE","defaultText":"Insert quote text here.","flipContent":null,"imageAltText":"photo (generic)","marginBottom":"bottom-large"},"type":"QUOTE","title":"Quote","pageId":"1f04f73e-4282-4e13-951a-80f26d67ec47","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":null,"createdAt":"2025-05-29T18:52:51.671+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":null,"postStructure":[],"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"29e5e774-91dd-492e-8072-dd805d85062e":{"id":"29e5e774-91dd-492e-8072-dd805d85062e","data":{"info":"\u003cp\u003eQuestions? Concerns? Need to Vent?\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eContact us at: \u003ca href=\"mailto:hello@ryanforillinois.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehello@ryanforillinois.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePO Box 68492 Schaumburg, IL 60168\u003c/p\u003e","bgColor":"bg4","marginTop":"top-large","disclaimer":"\u003cp\u003eRYAN VETTICAD IS A FORMER DOJ EMPLOYEE AND AIR FORCE ROTC CADET. USE OF HIS JOB TITLES, AND PHOTOGRAPHS IN UNIFORM DOES NOT IMPLY ENDORSEMENT BY THE JUSTICE DEPT. OR THE DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePAID FOR BY RYAN FOR ILLINOIS\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","quoteImage":"https://media.designedtorun.com/415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202/1654141695823-podpros-2mMhaoBGjCs-unsplash-.jpg","hideRunLink":false,"showPaidFor":true,"marginBottom":"bottom-large","poweredByText":"Powered by","showDescription":true,"shouldShowRunLogo":true},"type":"FOOTER","title":"Footer","pageId":"64f8fc66-90be-4ea2-93d4-45138d0762d2","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":null,"createdAt":"2025-05-29T18:52:51.671+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":"0e86911e-66b5-4bac-885c-f9676424d6e2","postStructure":[],"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"c0cf389c-27ed-42f4-87f2-e962bddc6a88":{"id":"c0cf389c-27ed-42f4-87f2-e962bddc6a88","data":{"text":"\u003ch2\u003eTerms and Conditions\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch3\u003eThis page notices our campaigns Terms and Conditions\u003c/h3\u003e\u003cp\u003eWelcome to the official website of RYANFORILLINOIS (the “Campaign,” “we,” “us,” or “our”). By accessing this website, signing up to receive communications, donating, volunteering, or otherwise interacting with us, you agree to the following Terms \u0026amp; Conditions. If you do not agree to these Terms, please do not use this website or sign up for communications.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUse of Website\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis website is intended to provide information about Ryan’s campaign, upcoming events, volunteer opportunities, and ways to support the Campaign. You agree to use this website only for lawful purposes and not to misuse, disrupt, or attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the website.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCampaign Communications\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBy submitting your contact information through our website, forms, event sign-ups, or other campaign channels, you consent to receive communications from RYANFORILLINOIS, which may include campaign updates, event invitations and reminders, volunteer opportunities, voter outreach information, fundraising and donation requests, and get-out-the-vote reminders. Communications may be delivered by email, phone call, or SMS/text message, depending on the information you provide.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSMS / Text Messaging Terms\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBy providing your mobile phone number and affirmatively opting in, you consent to receive recurring automated and non-automated text messages from RYANFORILLINOIS.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTypes of Messages You May Receive\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eText messages may include campaign updates and announcements, event invitations and reminders, volunteer coordination messages, polling or survey messages, donation and fundraising requests, and election reminders.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMessage Frequency\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMessage frequency will vary based on your interaction with the Campaign, but you may receive multiple messages per month. Message frequency may increase during election periods or around major campaign events.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eMessage and Data Rates\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eMessage and data rates may apply. Your mobile carrier’s standard messaging and data charges may apply to all SMS communications. Charges are billed by and payable to your mobile service provider.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOpt-Out Instructions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou may opt out at any time by replying STOP to cancel future messages or HELP for help or additional information. After you send STOP, you will receive a confirmation message and will no longer receive SMS messages from us unless you re-subscribe.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eConsent Not Required for Donation\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eConsent to receive text messages is not a condition of making a donation or supporting the Campaign.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePrivacy Policy\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYour privacy is important to us. Our data collection and usage practices are described in our Privacy Policy, available at: \u003ca href=\"https://www.ryanforillinois.com/privacy-policy\"\u003ehttps://www.ryanforillinois.com/privacy-policy\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe Privacy Policy explains what personal information we collect, how we use that information, how we protect your information, and your rights regarding your data.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe do not sell or share mobile opt-in data with third parties for marketing or promotional purposes. Mobile information will not be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes. Information sharing to subcontractors in support services, such as texting platforms, email distribution vendors, or data processors, is permitted solely for the purpose of providing services to the Campaign.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOpt-In Requirements\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBy entering your phone number into a Campaign form and checking the applicable consent box where required, you expressly agree to receive SMS communications from the Campaign. We do not use pre-checked consent boxes. Consent must be affirmative and explicit.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDonations and Financial Contributions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll donations are voluntary and subject to applicable federal and/or state campaign finance laws.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eBy making a donation, you certify that you are at least 18 years old, you are a U.S. citizen or lawful permanent resident, the funds you are donating are your own personal funds, you are not donating on behalf of another person, and you are not a federal government contractor if prohibited under applicable law.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDonations are not tax-deductible as charitable contributions. If you opt in to SMS communications, donation solicitations may be sent via text message.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThird-Party Service Providers\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe may use trusted third-party vendors such as texting platforms, CRM systems, fundraising platforms, and email service providers to assist in delivering communications and managing campaign operations. These providers are contractually obligated to safeguard your information and may only use it to provide services on our behalf.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eData Security\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your personal information. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or mobile networks is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIntellectual Property\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eAll content on this website, including text, logos, graphics, images, videos, and design, is the property of RYANFORILLINOIS unless otherwise noted and may not be reproduced without permission.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eProhibited Use\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou may not use this website for unlawful purposes, attempt to interfere with website functionality, submit false or misleading information, or impersonate another individual.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eChanges to These Terms\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe may update these Terms and Conditions at any time. Updates will be posted on this page with a revised effective date. Continued use of the website or Campaign services constitutes acceptance of any changes.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eContact Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you have questions about these Terms and Conditions or our communications practices, please contact:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eRYANFORILLINOIS - hello@ryanforillinois.com\u003c/p\u003e","bgColor":"bg0","eyebrow":"Eyebrow Text Here","headline":"Headline Text Here","marginTop":"top-large","headlineOn":false,"description":"Description Text Here","eyebrowSize":0,"showEyebrow":false,"headlineSize":0,"marginBottom":"bottom-large","descriptionSize":0,"showDescription":false},"type":"BASIC_TEXT","title":"Text","pageId":"fbbb0a61-aa6d-4d77-a941-dca6e8d25bb0","siteId":"f683133e-6417-446e-ac39-6479efbabbee","deleted":false,"variant":null,"createdAt":"2026-02-27T20:16:36.182349+00:00","published":true,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T16:51:03.873692+00:00","linkedBlockId":null,"postStructure":null,"primaryBlockId":null,"lastTranslatedAt":null},"29d0c38f-e658-4ff7-90bf-3c623041227c":{"id":"29d0c38f-e658-4ff7-90bf-3c623041227c","data":{"logo":"https://media.designedtorun.com/415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202/1654142639752-yournamelogo---runcbt::0,cbl::141.782131661442,cbw::419.435736677116,cbh::300,d::1662850822244,o::https:--slash----slash--media.designedtorun.com--slash--415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202--slash--1654142639752-yournamelogo-.pngrun--.png","action":true,"formId":"212f980f-b957-415e-8d55-715b8279da81","bgColor":"bg1","buttons":[{"id":"9b205b5d-021e-4561-8fda-34cde40ce609","url":"","buttonUrl":"","buttonText":"Learn More"}],"eyebrow":"Add your eyebrow here","headline":"Donate","linkSize":0,"navColor":"bg2","wrapForm":false,"embedCode":"","hasMargin":false,"marginTop":"top-large","actionType":"form","buttonSize":0,"buttonType":"underlined","headlineOn":true,"layoutType":"gradient_box","bigLogoSize":0,"buttonColor":"button-background","description":"Add your description here","eyebrowSize":0,"flipContent":false,"mobileImage":"","openSection":"Content","showBigLogo":false,"showEyebrow":false,"adjustLayout":"standard","alignContent":"content-center","desktopImage":"https://run.imgix.net/415b7455-174b-4f9e-9d05-7c9dbda44202/26fa80a0-1164-42d6-9286-45e711b74785/26fa80a0-1164-42d6-9286-45e711b74785.jpeg?ixlib=js-3.8.0\u0026bri=0\u0026con=